## What it does

`packages/devtools` adds `rat_*` capabilities to a development composition. They list, read, dispatch, replay, and diff capability calls. `CallWatch` surrounds the approval-gated handler, including denied calls. `watchActor` lets lifecycle machines report states and events through `ActorWatch`. Both watchers default to no-ops without the recording layer.

The local web development backend records calls and serves the overlay, RPC, and MCP tools under `/__rat`. The CLI enables its devtools surfaces with `--devtools`, bound to loopback only. These capabilities are available only in development.

## The standard

- Tools dispatch through the existing capability's schemas and handler.
- Recorder code and test people stay in development compositions and tests.
- Every Effect-backed lifecycle actor is handed to `watchActor`.
- Production bundles contain no web development modules, devtools code, or test people.

## How to check

- Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/devtools test` for recording and tool behavior.
- Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/web test` for the local backend and production-bundle exclusion test.
- Run `pnpm lint` for `no-devtools-in-production` and `watch-effect-actors`.
- Inspect `rat_list_actors`, `rat_list_transitions`, and `rat_get_actor` in a development composition after running a lifecycle capability. Without a recording layer, these tools cannot show whether a lifecycle ran.
